      "category": "Text",
      "text": "§ 2. All mayoral agencies shall, whenever practicable, use their discretion under section 311(i) of the New York City Charter to limit the pool of solicited vendors for goods, services and construction for amounts not exceeding $500,000 to Black American M/WBEs, Hispanic American M/WBEs, Native American M/WBEs and Asian American WBEs. The Mayor's Office of Minority and Women-Owned Business Enterprises (“OM/WBE”) shall issue guidance on the process of prioritizing, where practicable, these most underutilized categories of M/WBEs for such solicitations.",
      "logprob_stats": {
